<https://w3id.org/aooe#> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-10-27"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Map> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionLevel> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#useCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Rulebook> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Grants agency. Only data governed at Rulebook level may be acted on by an agent (Core Rule 8). The Lab-private compilation layer (rewards, traces, benchmarks, curriculum releases) is the top of the Rulebook, not a fourth level."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#includesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The lower level a level contains. Levels are cumulative: claiming a level claims every level it includes."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#reuseMode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "identity: the term and IRI are reused and property characteristics are added locally; axioms: the source axiomatization is adopted as well."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#reuseMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reuse mode"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#useCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionRecord> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptsLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "adopts level"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Legend> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The vocabulary reference: which external vocabularies are reused, at which verified versions, under which prefixes, and how instance identifiers are minted. Done when every import is pinned and verified, every prefix binds to one IRI, pins live only in the import manifest, and the identity policy is written."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A cumulative conformance level of the AOOE methodology. Each level has its own definition of done and its own gate subset."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#termsReused> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The external terms a bundle actually wires into its ontology body. A term listed here but never used is manifest drift (gate C4)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#servesACQ> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "serves agent competency question"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adopter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionRecord> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Rulebook> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rulebook"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adopter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#useCase> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#includesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#reuseMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#providesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Optional in v0.7 (absent is reported as undeclared); required from v0.8."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "0.7.0" .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptedSince> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "adopted since"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Map> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Grants readability and analysis. A Map-level consumer can load and query the data. It cannot let an agent act on it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#termsReused> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Legend> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Grants addressability. A Legend-level consumer can read and name the data. It cannot claim the data model or any validation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#includesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "includes level"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Legend> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legend"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adopter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The team, system or organisation unit that adopts."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#providesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/rights> "Copyright WordLift. This vocabulary is released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0). The AOOE methodology, its tooling and templates are maintained separately and are not covered by this licence."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Terms the AOOE methodology uses to annotate import manifests, Behavioral Concept Specifications and adoption levels. This is a methodology vocabulary, not a domain vocabulary: it never appears in a public projection."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptedSince> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Map> <https://w3id.org/aooe#includesLevel> <https://w3id.org/aooe#Legend> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#refines> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#refines> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Links a refinement BCS to its parent; definition of done is parent plus delta, and the delta may only tighten."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#pinnedVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A pin is verified, never asserted. An unverifiable pin is written UNVERIFIED-<date> and reported."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptsLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionRecord> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#servesACQ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The competency question(s) that justify an import."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#governanceNote> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#includesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#providesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionLevel> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#governanceNote> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "governance note"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#termsReused> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Carried as a comma-separated CURIE string (v0.3 convention) or as repeated IRIs (v0.6 convention)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#governs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "governs"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <https://wordlift.io/> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "AOOE — Agent-Oriented Ontology Engineering vocabulary"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One row of a bundle's adoption register: who adopts, for which use case, at which level, since when, pinned to which release."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#pinnedVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The verified version of an imported vocabulary, stated on the vocabulary IRI (v0.6 convention). The v0.3 convention states owl:versionInfo on the annotation block instead; both are accepted."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Rulebook> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionLevel> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptedRelease> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#reuseMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#includesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionLevel> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#governanceNote> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptedSince> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionRecord> .
