<https://w3id.org/aooe#refines> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "refines"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#providesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "provides level"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptedRelease> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionRecord> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptsLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The level a consumer claims for one use case."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptedSince> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#pinnedVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pinned version"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptedRelease> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#useCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "use case"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#importedVocabulary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "imported vocabulary"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#pinnedVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Rulebook> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Validation and behavior: SHACL shapes, negative examples, Behavioral Concept Specifications, policy envelopes, gates, eval items and reward specs. Done when Map is done and the full definition of done holds: shapes target the class, positives conform, negatives fail independently, the non-vacuity sentinel passes, the BCS has eleven sections, the envelope is signed, and eval and reward execute."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Adoption record"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#servesACQ> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#governs> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Links a BCS to the behavioral class whose instances it governs."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#termsReused> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "terms reused"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptedRelease> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The release tag of the bundle the adopter pins (for example core/v0.2.0)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adopter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "adopter"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#includesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aooe#AdoptionLevel> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Map> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The data model: classes, properties, application profiles, qualified relations and locally added property characteristics. Done when Legend is done, every term carries a label and a definition, reused external terms are wired, no external property carries a local domain or range, the module is reasoner-consistent, and at least one positive example uses the term with only declared terms."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#providesLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The highest adoption level a package (an ontology module, bundle or brand layer) ships and proves. The gate runner refuses a declared level the package does not pass."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#importedVocabulary> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#governs> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#adoptsLevel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#pinnedVersion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Rulebook> <https://w3id.org/aooe#includesLevel> <https://w3id.org/aooe#Map> .
<https://w3id.org/aooe#Map> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Map"@en .
